Authorized X-items (tasks.md):

- X-2 `tests/TaxAI.Portal.Tests/Upgrade/UpgradeBaselineContractTests.cs` — the
  two overloads by exact signature, `Persistence.DevelopmentFixtureIdentity`,
  `TaxAI.Portal.DevelopmentSignInEndpoints`, and
  `Components.Pages.DevelopmentSignInPage`.
- X-4 `tests/Persistence.Tests/Contracts/PersistenceContractTests.cs` — exports
  are the registration class and the constants class; the registration class
  has exactly the two approved overloads.
- X-5 `PortalSecurityTests.cs` authentication allowlists and enumerated file
  set, and `CompositionRootTests.cs` concern vocabulary (now exactly five).

Additional narrow amendment, authorized by the human on 2026-10-01 after the
gate exposed it (it is not one of X-1 to X-7):

- `PortalBoundaryTests.TheCompositionRootCallsExactlyOneRegistrationExtensionPerContributingModule`
  — the count of `AddTaxAiPersistence` declarations in Persistence is re-pinned
  from 1 to 2, because T01 adds the already-approved overload. The
  architectural guarantee is preserved: Persistence declares exactly the two
  approved overloads; the portal composition root still calls the Persistence
  registration extension exactly once, which the same test still asserts; no
  additional registration entry point is authorized; and the
  contributing-module and composition-root assertions are otherwise unchanged.

Every amended guard keeps its existing test method names, except one test that
no ledger references and whose name would have become false:
`SeederCreatesNoIdentityMembershipSessionOrCredentialRow` is now
`SeederCreatesExactlyOneSyntheticUserAndMembershipAndNoSessionOrCredential`.
`AmendmentAuditTests.cs` is not edited.

Guards listed for T01 that needed no edit: `ConnectionStringGuardTests.cs`,
`PersistenceBoundaryTests.cs`, `RouteAuthenticationBaselineTests.cs`,
